{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he arose in the night.</b> He intended to flee by another route." "<b>And he arose in the night, he.</b> The word הוא cuts it short — 'he arose in the night.' <b>And he took his two wives and his two maidservants and his eleven children</b> — he put the women before the children, because he was more protective of his sons than of his wives: if Esau came to kill, he would kill the women first. But when he fled from Laban's house, he put the children before the women, so that when Laban pursued him he would encounter his daughters first." "<b>Yabbok.</b> One may say: it is the Jordan mentioned above — 'I crossed this Jordan' — and here its name is Yabbok."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:07.512501427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}